Third-party material

1. ArduPilot's Gazebo plugin. The folders study1/ardupilot/gazebo/ardupilot_gazebo/
   and study2/ardupilot/gazebo/ardupilot_gazebo/ hold the same files. Each holds files added to a local checkout of https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot_gazebo
   at commit f116b035, which is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public
   License, version 3 (LICENSES/LGPL-3.0.txt, which supplements
   LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt). These files keep that licence:

     models/iris_cine/ and models/iris_cine_standoffs/, adapted from the
     plugin's iris_with_ardupilot and iris_with_standoffs models (their authors
     are listed in each model.config);
     CMakeLists.patch, a change to the plugin's CMakeLists.txt that leaves out
     the camera-streaming plugins.

   The three world files in that folder (cine_splits_arena.sdf,
   cine_splits_field3x.sdf, course3d-7-cam.sdf) were written for this project
   and load the plugin's models.

2. Gazebo Fuel models. The other folders under
   ardupilot/gazebo/ardupilot_gazebo/models/, in study1/ and in study2/, hold model definitions
   (model.sdf and model.config) adapted from models published on
   https://fuel.gazebosim.org by Open Robotics. Depot, from which cine_depot and
   cine_arena_hall are built, is licensed under CC BY 4.0. Collapsed Fire
   Station, Collapsed House, Collapsed Industrial Building, Construction Barrel,
   Construction Cone, Gas Station, Power Plant, Tower Crane, Truss Bridge and
   Water Tower are licensed under CC0 1.0 (licences read from Fuel on 7 November
   2026). Their authors are listed in each model.config. No meshes or textures
   are included; Gazebo downloads them from Fuel. cine_field_ground was written
   for this project; its texture, ambientCG Ground037, is CC0 1.0 and is not
   included.

3. The Split-S track. The seven gate positions and the start position in
   ardupilot/course_splits.py, in study1/ and in study2/, are copied from tracks/track.yaml in
   https://github.com/uzh-rpg/rpg_time_optimal (University of Zurich, Robotics
   and Perception Group), which is licensed under the GNU General Public
   License, version 3 (LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt). They describe the track published
   in Foehn P, Romero A and Scaramuzza D (2021) 'Time-optimal planning for
   quadrotor waypoint flight', Science Robotics 6(56):eabh1221,
   doi:10.1126/scirobotics.abh1221.

4. The learning core. study1/protocol/telohelm-0.1.0.dev0-py3-none-any.whl is
   Telohelm's learning core, by the same author under the MIT License. Its
   Python source is identical to Telohelm 0.1.0,
   https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23993336.
   study2/protocol/telohelm-0.1.0.dev0+paper3.2-py3-none-any.whl is the same
   core with study2/protocol/wheel3/sandbox.patch applied to
   telohelm/runtime/sandbox.py. Each wheel also holds three files
   copied unmodified from the Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B model repository at revision
   1d4bf0f2ff6012fd82039f2fa52739d0dd7c60c0, published by the Qwen team under
   the Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt):

     telohelm/model_files/Qwen3.8-27B-1d4bf0f2ff6012fd82039f2fa52739d0dd7c60c0/tokenizer.json
       SHA-256 0997f410c57a1f4e53b09e4be8f4a172d90edd9564368fb0847030937229b9f3
     telohelm/model_files/Qwen3.8-27B-1d4bf0f2ff6012fd82039f2fa52739d0dd7c60c0/tokenizer_config.json
       SHA-256 b11349aafa7cdc6a320767cf7ceb29ed82f7eda5d65e8e0819e76f0ce947bf27
     telohelm/model_files/Qwen3.8-27B-1d4bf0f2ff6012fd82039f2fa52739d0dd7c60c0/chat_template.jinja
